      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "H2: finite formal tuple vectors are encoded into polynomial ideals so that the generalized Hilbert theorem controls increasing equivariant subspace chains; stabilization then produces a finite test set for weighted-register zeroness. The actual theorem gives a finite testing characterization over reducts of well-structured ordered domains. The author's subsequent computability-qualified remark is retained, without promoting it to unqualified decidability or recounting prior equality/ordered cases.",
